  "concept_reviews": [
    {
      "block": 12,
      "source_text": "我们利用在方程的左边配一个二项式的平方的方法（简称：配方法），再解几个 $ax^2+bx+c=0$（$a\\neq0$）这种形式的方程。",
      "independent_interpretation": "Completing the square turns the quadratic equation into an equivalent equation with the square of a binomial, which is then solved with all admissible square-root branches.",
      "independent_algebra": "For z^2+pz+q=0, moving q and adding p^2/4 to both sides gives (z+p/2)^2=p^2/4-q. Over the reals, a positive right side gives two distinct roots, zero gives one distinct repeated root, and a negative right side gives no roots.",
      "fidelity_need": "Exercise 855 expressly requires this method. Merely recognizing a correct final root list does not by itself demonstrate the specified completing-square relationship. Later views must be assessed for genuine judgment of the equivalent square and its consequences, with any production-to-recognition loss recorded."
    },
    {
      "block": 28,
      "source_text": "用 $x^2$ 的系数除方程的两边，得到和已知方程同解的简化的二次方程：",
      "independent_interpretation": "Divide every term on both sides by the nonzero leading coefficient to obtain a monic quadratic with exactly the same solutions.",
      "independent_algebra": "az^2+bz+c=0 with a!=0 is equivalent to z^2+(b/a)z+c/a=0. Completing the square then gives (z+b/(2a))^2=(b^2-4ac)/(4a^2). The division must affect both the linear coefficient and the constant.",
      "fidelity_need": "Normalization is relevant to both equations in 856. Their source instruction only says to solve, so another valid solving method is not a source-fidelity failure. If a visible question tests normalization or completing the square, the equivalence and fractional coefficients must be correct."
    }
  ],
